  "description": "We would like to create a series of raised beds for growing herbs and plants with medicinal uses as a reference to the Abbey’s history and which will be planted and maintained by the local community. The design should take into consideration the correct height for people with mobility issues to access including seats / perches for people to use when gardening. An Interpretation board highlighting the planting choices and background of the use of medicinal plants in the Abbey should form part of the design.\nMaterials to be chosen for longevity and should blend with existing materials on site – stone walling and coping, corten steel, Yorkstone paving etc. The design should incorporate surrounding planting (hedge and trees) so that any new construction and installations do not cause damage.\nCommunity involvement will be at each stage of the design project as they contribute to the design brief, approving the design, possible trips to similar sites such as Lewes Abbey, giving input into the planting choices and in particular the level of ongoing maintenance.\n",
